      ":question/worked-solution": "Remember that $\\mathbb{Q}_0^{+}$ is the set of all positive rational numbers and zero.\n\n- $-\\frac{8}{3}$: It is negative, and it is a rational number but not an integer. Therefore, it does *not* belong to $\\mathbb{Q}_0^{+}$.\n\n- $70$: It is positive, and it is an integer. Therefore, it belongs to $\\mathbb{Q}_0^{+}$.\n\n- $\\frac{30}{5}=6$: It is positive, and it is an integer. Therefore, it belongs to $\\mathbb{Q}_0^{+}$.\n\n- $8.4=\\frac{42}{5}$: It is positive, and it is a rational number but not an integer, since it can be written as $\\frac{42}{5}$. Therefore, it belongs to $\\mathbb{Q}_0^{+}$.\n\nIn conclusion, the correct answer is: $70$; $\\frac{30}{5}$; $8.4$.",
