      ":question/problem": "Which of the numbers below belong to $\\mathbb{R}_0^{-}$?\n\nSelect all that apply.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Remember that $\\mathbb{R}_0^{-}$ is the set of all negative real numbers and zero.\n\n- $7.5=\\frac{15}{2}$: It is positive, and it is a rational number but not an integer, since it can be written as $\\frac{15}{2}$. Therefore, it does *not* belong to $\\mathbb{R}_0^{-}$.\n\n- $2$: It is positive, and it is an integer. Therefore, it does *not* belong to $\\mathbb{R}_0^{-}$.\n\n- $\\sqrt{25}=5$: It is positive, and it is an integer. Therefore, it does *not* belong to $\\mathbb{R}_0^{-}$.\n\n- $\\sqrt{39}$: It is positive, and it is an irrational real number. Therefore, it does *not* belong to $\\mathbb{R}_0^{-}$.\n\nIn conclusion, the correct answer is: None of those listed.",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
