      ":question/id": "a4c446c8-0fae-5f38-adbd-ce230fa8b124",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the numbers below belong to $\\mathbb{Z}_0^{-}$?\n\nSelect all that apply.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Remember that $\\mathbb{Z}_0^{-}$ is the set of all negative integers and zero.\n\n- $0$: Zero is included by the subscript $0$. Therefore, it belongs to $\\mathbb{Z}_0^{-}$.\n\n- $\\frac{17}{4}$: It is positive, and it is a rational number but not an integer. Therefore, it does *not* belong to $\\mathbb{Z}_0^{-}$.\n\n- $-\\pi$: It is negative, and it is an irrational real number. Therefore, it does *not* belong to $\\mathbb{Z}_0^{-}$.\n\n- $1.5=\\frac{3}{2}$: It is positive, and it is a rational number but not an integer, since it can be written as $\\frac{3}{2}$. Therefore, it does *not* belong to $\\mathbb{Z}_0^{-}$.\n\nIn conclusion, the correct answer is: $0$.",
