      ":question/problem": "Which of the numbers below belong to $\\mathbb{Q}^{-}$?\n\nSelect all that apply.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Remember that $\\mathbb{Q}^{-}$ is the set of all negative rational numbers.\n\n- $-40$: It is negative, and it is an integer. Therefore, it belongs to $\\mathbb{Q}^{-}$.\n\n- $4.9=\\frac{49}{10}$: It is positive, and it is a rational number but not an integer, since it can be written as $\\frac{49}{10}$. Therefore, it does *not* belong to $\\mathbb{Q}^{-}$.\n\n- $3\\sqrt{7}$: It is positive, and it is an irrational real number. Therefore, it does *not* belong to $\\mathbb{Q}^{-}$.\n\n- $-\\sqrt{49}=-7$: It is negative, and it is an integer. Therefore, it belongs to $\\mathbb{Q}^{-}$.\n\nIn conclusion, the correct answer is: $-40$; $-\\sqrt{49}$.",
