    "question": {
      ":question/id": "e6abab5d-12fd-5968-aa58-bb1b06bb680e",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the numbers below belong to $\\mathbb{Z}_0^{-}$?\n\nSelect all that apply.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Remember that $\\mathbb{Z}_0^{-}$ is the set of all negative integers and zero.\n\n- $0$: Zero is included by the subscript $0$. Therefore, it belongs to $\\mathbb{Z}_0^{-}$.\n\n- $-\\sqrt{36}=-6$: It is negative, and it is an integer. Therefore, it belongs to $\\mathbb{Z}_0^{-}$.\n\n- $\\sqrt{48}=4\\sqrt{3}$: It is positive, and it is an irrational real number. Therefore, it does *not* belong to $\\mathbb{Z}_0^{-}$.\n\n- $\\pi$: It is positive, and it is an irrational real number. Therefore, it does *not* belong to $\\mathbb{Z}_0^{-}$.\n\nIn conclusion, the correct answer is: $0$; $-\\sqrt{36}$.",
