      ":question/worked-solution": "Remember that $\\mathbb{Z}_0^{-}$ is the set of all negative integers and zero.\n\n- $\\frac{20}{2}=10$: It is positive, and it is an integer. Therefore, it does *not* belong to $\\mathbb{Z}_0^{-}$.\n\n- $-\\sqrt{49}=-7$: It is negative, and it is an integer. Therefore, it belongs to $\\mathbb{Z}_0^{-}$.\n\n- $-3\\sqrt{7}$: It is negative, and it is an irrational real number. Therefore, it does *not* belong to $\\mathbb{Z}_0^{-}$.\n\n- $-\\frac{28}{7}=-4$: It is negative, and it is an integer. Therefore, it belongs to $\\mathbb{Z}_0^{-}$.\n\nIn conclusion, the correct answer is: $-\\sqrt{49}$; $-\\frac{28}{7}$.",
